>> title: Herb Knot Bread
>> servings: 8
>> author: Ted Lin
>> date: 2020-07-27
>> dish: herb bread
>> keywords: bread, garlic, herbs, sourdough discard
>> summary: A messy loaf packed with garlic and herbs, like pizza-shop breadsticks; measurements are by feel.
>> image: static/photos/herb-knot-bread/knot_mess.jpg

# Dough

:mix @{all-purpose flour|4 cups}, @{bread flour|1 cup}, @{yeast|1 tsp}, @{salt|2 tsp} in #bowl => _flour.
:combine @{warm water|1 1/2 cups}, @{sourdough discard|1/2 cup|straight from the fridge} => _liquid.
:{rest|a few minutes} _liquid, then check for yeast activity.
:mix and knead _liquid, _flour, @{oil|3 tbsp} until smooth => _dough.
  (add flour if it is too wet for you, but it should be sticky and tacky)
:{proof|about 1 hour} _dough in #{oiled bowl} until roughly doubled.

# Shape

:punch down _dough and separate into at least 2 portions => _{dough portions}.
:roll _{dough portions} into rectangles; the size is arbitrary, a 5:3 ratio worked.
:slather @{herbs|whatever|finely chopped; basil, thyme, rosemary, garlic} and @oil on _{dough portions}, fold lengthwise in thirds.
:stack _{dough portions}, then shape into whatever you want => _loaf.
  (steamed-bun knots, rough braids, lengthwise slices braided, or a plain wet mess all work)
:place _loaf on a #{sheet pan} or #parchment.
:{rest|about 1 hour} _loaf.

# Bake

:preheat #{oven|400F} during the rest.
:{bake|about 20 min} _loaf.
:{rest|until cool} _loaf before slicing.

>> note: Leftover garlic aioli (garlic, oil, and salt pounded into an emulsion) is wonderful mixed into the herbs, or brushed over the bread after baking.
